<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CEZ IAS net profit rises, CAS down.</title>
<headline>Czech CEZ IAS net profit rises, CAS down.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited results for year</p>
<p>ending December 31, 1996: (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO INTERNATIONAL ACCOUNTING STANDARD (IAS)</p>
<p> Net profit		  9.71     vs    8.06</p>
<p> Operating revenues     55.385    vs   50.640</p>
<p> Operating expenses     39.281    vs   33.477</p>
<p> Operating income	 16.105    vs   17.163</p>
<p> Income before tax	15.646    vs   16.808</p>
<p> Income tax		  5.940    vs    7.503</p>
<p>Earnings per share with a nominal</p>
<p>  value of CZK 1,100    180 CZK   vs   173 CZK</p>
<p> Return on equity	 10.4 pct  vs   11.1 pct</p>
<p> P/E			   5.4	vs    5.6</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO CZECH ACCOUNTING STANDARDS (CAS)  Net profit		  7.848    vs    8.064</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	   12.680    vs   14.783</p>
<p> Total revenues	   60.252    vs   54.096</p>
<p> Total expenditure	47.572    vs   39.313</p>
<p>Earnings per share with a nominal</p>
<p>  value of CZK 1,100    145.9 CZK vs  150.0 CZK</p>
<p> Total Assets	    158.259    vs  138.174</p>
<p> Basic capital	    59.156    vs   59.131</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is CEZ a.s., the country's largest electricity generator.</p>
<p>The statement noted that total assets and basic capital figures are identincal for both international and Czech accounting standards.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
